TCG_CALL_NO_RWG on pure SSE/MMX helpers (Android fe63db36, header part only).
add/sub/mul/div/min/max/sqrt (ps/pd/ss/sd), hadd/hsub/addsub, all cmp*
variants, shufps/shufpd, the cvt* family, pack*/punpck*, pmaddwd and psadbw only
read and write the vector registers and sse_status through their pointer
arguments and never raise, so TCG may keep guest globals in host registers
across the call instead of spilling and reloading them.
Every body was re-checked in DukeX's target/i386/ops_sse.h: none touches a TCG
global (regs, eip, cc_*, seg bases, bnd, fpstt), calls GETPC/raise or loads from
guest memory. None dropped; the header is byte-identical to Android's base, so
this is Android's diff unchanged. Android claims no performance number.

